<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Hyperparameter Tuning</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To achieve the reported batch sizes, we employed gradient accumulation.
Tables <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.1 Hyperparameter Tuning ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ SpaRE: Enhancing Spatial Reasoning in Vision-Language Models with Synthetic Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ A.1 Hyperparameter Tuning ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ SpaRE: Enhancing Spatial Reasoning in Vision-Language Models with Synthetic Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> summarize the hyperparameter search and the selected values for training the <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SpaRE-2B</span> and <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SpaRE-7B</span> models respectively.
The search includes variations in learning rate (LR), batch size, epochs, optimizer, warm-up steps, dropout rate, and learning rate schedule.
For both models, the optimal values were chosen based on performance on a held-out subset.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
